# 
# 
# ---- What to take away ---------------------------------------------------------
# 
# - A vector holds one type. Mixing types coerces silently, upward:
#   Character > Double > Integer > Logical.
# - Anything you can select, you can assign to.
# - R recycles a short vector to match a long one, and only warns when the lengths
#   do not divide evenly.
# - `NA` is unknown, `NaN` is not a number, `Inf` is infinite. `is.na()` is `TRUE`
#   for the first two.
# - A matrix is a vector with a `dim`; a factor is an integer vector with `levels`
#   and a `class`. Attributes are what make them different.
# - `*` is elementwise, `%*%` is the matrix product.
# 
# ---- Going further -------------------------------------------------------------
# 
# The [appendix](appendix.qmd) covers the remaining atomic types, integer versus
# double storage, `structure()` in more depth, arrays, and why `solve()` is the
# same operation as fitting a regression.
